name=HARMONIE - From Garden to Plate
id=HARMONIE_GardenToPlate
description=Adds a vitamin (A, B, C, D, E, K) micronutrient system on top of the food you eat. Press N (rebindable) to check your own or a nearby survivor's nutritional status -- requires First Aid 5 to interpret the result. Neglect your diet and critical vitamin deficiencies will start to hurt you. Also adds home canning: preserve vegetables and fruit indefinitely in empty tin cans. Also adds a "Vitamins" tab right in the vanilla character info window -- shows Critical/Low/Sufficient at a glance for everyone, plus exact numbers at First Aid 3 and a top-10 food list per vitamin at Cooking 3 or with the Nutritionist trait. Also adds a green Vitamin Guide window (press N -- rebindable from the window's gear button --, a button in the character window's Vitamins tab, or with the Nutritional Assessment window): a Check tab for yourself or a nearby survivor (more detail with higher First Aid), what each vitamin deficiency does, every food that gives each vitamin with its picture, a full food table with a search box (amounts need Cooking 3 or the Nutritionist trait, like the food tooltip), vitamin pills, home canning and tips. Requires "Moodle Framework" (Workshop 3396446795) for per-vitamin moodles when Low or Critical, and "Modern Status" (Workshop 3451167732) for selectable per-vitamin HUD indicators -- please subscribe to both. Includes "Fruit Farming (B42)" by leina (Workshop 3779625821), used with credit: grow 14 vanilla fruits (apple, avocado, banana, cherry, grapefruit, grapes, lemon, lime, mango, olive, orange, peach, pear, pineapple), rice, coffee, ginger and peanuts, so every vitamin can be farmed. Do not enable Fruit Farming itself at the same time (it is built in). Also: vitamin D from sunlight, dried fruit, bean sprouts, fish liver oil, lemon and lime canning, fruit seeds in seed loot, a planting calendar in the guide, and a Cooking tab: 35 ready-made dishes made through the game's own cooking recipes, with preparation steps (wash, peel, chop, stir, season ...) played as short minigames that need the right tools and Cooking level; nutrition stays vanilla's and vitamins carry over.
